        "original_id": "b591d627-2481-5d21-9bfc-bca48250bdd1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Thomas Boutflower Bennett\n- Organizations: St Peter's College, Adelaide; J. L. Young's Adelaide Educational Institution\n- Places: South Australia; Adelaide\n- Roles: schoolmaster; early colonist\n\nFacts:\n- Thomas Boutflower Bennett was born in 1808 and died on 14 September 1894.\n- Thomas Boutflower Bennett was an early colonist of South Australia.\n- Thomas Boutflower Bennett is remembered as a schoolmaster at J. L. Young's Adelaide Educational Institution.\n- Thomas Boutflower Bennett is remembered as a schoolmaster at St Peter's College in Adelaide.\n- St Peter's College is officially named The Collegiate School of St Peter.\n- St Peter's College is commonly known as SPSC, Sancti Petri Schola Collegiata, St Peter's, and Saints.\n- St Peter's College is an independent boys' school in Adelaide, the capital of South Australia.",
